---
// Positioning.astro — Explicit positioning against adjacent categories
---

<section id="positioning" class="section-pad positioning-section">
  <div class="section-inner">
    <span class="section-eyebrow" data-reveal>WHERE KITARU FITS</span>
    <h2 class="section-title" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="1">
      The lifecycle layer. Nothing else.
    </h2>
    <p class="positioning-desc" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="2">
      We're not trying to replace the tools your team already uses. Agent frameworks, sandboxes, orchestrators, observability &mdash; they all play a role. Kitaru is the layer between them that almost no one else provides.
    </p>

    <div class="positioning-grid">

      <div class="positioning-card" data-reveal="scale-up" data-reveal-delay="3">
        <div class="card-glow"></div>
        <div class="positioning-label">Not a framework</div>
        <h3>We don't replace LangGraph, PydanticAI, or the Agent SDKs.</h3>
        <p>Use whatever framework your team picks. Kitaru wraps it.</p>
        <div class="positioning-tools">
          <span class="positioning-tool">LangGraph</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">PydanticAI</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">CrewAI</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="positioning-card" data-reveal="scale-up" data-reveal-delay="4">
        <div class="card-glow"></div>
        <div class="positioning-label">Not a sandbox</div>
        <h3>We don't replace Daytona, E2B, or Modal.</h3>
        <p>Configure your sandbox in your agent code. Kitaru observes what happens inside.</p>
        <div class="positioning-tools">
          <span class="positioning-tool">Daytona</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">E2B</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">Modal</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="positioning-card" data-reveal="scale-up" data-reveal-delay="5">
        <div class="card-glow"></div>
        <div class="positioning-label">Not an orchestrator</div>
        <h3>We don't replace Temporal or Prefect.</h3>
        <p>Your Runner handles the loop. We can be the Runner, but don't have to be.</p>
        <div class="positioning-tools">
          <span class="positioning-tool">Temporal</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">Prefect</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">Dagster</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="positioning-card" data-reveal="scale-up" data-reveal-delay="6">
        <div class="card-glow"></div>
        <div class="positioning-label">Not observability</div>
        <h3>We don't replace LangSmith, Langfuse, or Braintrust.</h3>
        <p>They score traces. Kitaru is the infrastructure those traces live in &mdash; versioned, lineaged, governed.</p>
        <div class="positioning-tools">
          <span class="positioning-tool">Langfuse</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">Braintrust</span>
          <span class="positioning-tool">LangSmith</span>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <p class="positioning-conclusion" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="7">
      Kitaru is <strong>what happens between your agent SDK and your production cloud</strong> &mdash; the deploy, the checkpoints, the artifacts, the lineage, the governance. The glue that lets everything else do what it does best.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .positioning-section {
    background: var(--color-bg);
  }

  .positioning-desc {
    max-width: 720px;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.15rem);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    margin-top: 16px;
    margin-bottom: 48px;
  }

  .positioning-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .positioning-card {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 28px;
    transition: border-color 0.3s;
  }

  .positioning-card:hover {
    border-color: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.25);
  }

  .positioning-card:hover .card-glow {
    opacity: 1;
  }

  .positioning-label {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    padding: 4px 10px;
    background: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.08);
    border: 1px solid oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.2);
    border-radius: 100px;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .positioning-card h3 {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.35;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
    color: var(--color-primary);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  .positioning-card p {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--color-secondary);
    font-weight: 300;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .positioning-tools {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 6px;
  }

  .positioning-tool {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.68rem;
    padding: 3px 10px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    background: var(--color-surface-warm);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .positioning-conclusion {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding: 28px 32px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-accent);
    background: oklch(0.65 0.16 45 / 0.04);
    border-radius: 0 10px 10px 0;
    font-size: clamp(0.98rem, 1.5vw, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .positioning-conclusion strong {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .positioning-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .positioning-card {
      padding: 24px;
    }

    .positioning-conclusion {
      padding: 22px 24px;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { setupCardGlow } from '../scripts/card-glow';
  setupCardGlow('#positioning .positioning-card');
</script>
